LRC14 CURRIED PACKET FUNCTIONAL TOWER
status: synthesis scout / proof-interface guardrail, not a proof

Core total evaluator:
  E : S -> P(S) -> root -> lane -> fiber -> certificate -> verdict
  A quotient is a partial evaluation of E plus a declared lost-coordinate function.

Quotient audit law:
  lost_Q(coord)(y)(x,x') = coord(x) - coord(x') on the fiber Q^-1(y)
  allowed iff lost_Q is zero, reconstructed, coboundary/exact,
  dual-annihilated, descended to a family, AP/GW boundary equality,
  or routed to F7/THM-572 residual debt.

Fibonacci path-rank partial evaluations:
  A(2)(k) row=1            sum=1
  A(3)(k) row=1+1          sum=2
  A(4)(k) row=1+2          sum=3
  A(5)(k) row=1+3+1        sum=5
  A(6)(k) row=1+4+3        sum=8
  A(7)(k) row=1+5+6+1      sum=13
  A(8)(k) row=1+6+10+4     sum=21
  A(9)(k) row=1+7+15+10+1  sum=34

LRC14 unit-excess Farey partial evaluations p -> q -> lane:
  F(1)(13): root=(1, 13, 1), sum=14, product=13, power_digit_lengths=(2, 1)
  F(2)(27): root=(2, 27, 1), sum=29, product=54, power_digit_lengths=(3, 9)
  F(3)(41): root=(3, 41, 1), sum=44, product=123, power_digit_lengths=(5, 20)
  F(4)(55): root=(4, 55, 1), sum=59, product=220, power_digit_lengths=(7, 34)
  F(5)(69): root=(5, 69, 1), sum=74, product=345, power_digit_lengths=(10, 49)
  F(6)(83): root=(6, 83, 1), sum=89, product=498, power_digit_lengths=(12, 65)

Named-row curried readout templates:
  AP:
    call:    E(AP)(boundary_packet)(e=0)(root/sum)(same_tile)(no-open)
    verdict: AP/GW boundary equality atom
  GW:
    call:    E(GW)(C27_boundary_packet)(e=0)(root/sum)(same_tile)(no-open)
    verdict: AP/GW boundary equality atom with C27 transfer label
  K33 12->36:
    call:    E(row)(K33_packet)(p=3)(product)(cross_handoff)(Fejer d159)
    verdict: strict-safe certificate or named K33/state-lift debt
  P10+GW:
    call:    E(row)(unit_petal_packet)(root)(sum/product)(owner_strip)(Fejer d280)
    verdict: strict-safe certificate after petal/GW labels are retained
  covering 12->84:
    call:    E(row)(covering_packet)(root)(sum)(nested_refinement)(boundary_moment)
    verdict: positive covering/boundary-moment packet, not scalar all-covered

Function-carrier retention vectors
features: predicate, fiber_labels, argument_order, dual_certificate, residual_name, farey_scale, additive_carry, anti_scalar
  total_curried_packet_evaluator: (3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3)
    type:    S -> P(S) -> root -> lane -> fiber -> certificate -> verdict
    partial: E(S)(packet)(p/q,e)(farey_lane)(fiber)(cert)
    LRC:     Keeps the full LRC proof object live until the last certificate.
    warning: Forgets nothing until a named discharge is returned.
  quotient_cocycle_derivative: (3, 3, 3, 2, 3, 2, 2, 3)
    type:    Q -> y -> (x,x' in fiber_y) -> lost_coordinate_delta
    partial: d_Q(coord)(y)(x,x')
    LRC:     Turns every quotient into an explicit lost-coordinate function.
    warning: Forgets the coordinate only after zero/coboundary/dual/residual tests.
  residual_section_router: (3, 3, 2, 2, 3, 2, 1, 3)
    type:    packet -> section -> grid_exit -> next_certificate_family
    partial: R(packet)(section)(owner_strip/cross/nested)
    LRC:     Routes HYP-2963 packets through HYP-2996 residual sections.
    warning: Forgets phase location after owner/cross/nested exit is labelled.
  fejer_toeplitz_dual_functional: (3, 2, 2, 3, 2, 1, 1, 3)
    type:    S -> k -> divisor_fiber -> coefficient -> quadratic_form
    partial: Phi(S)(k)(v|k)(atom_bank)
    LRC:     Makes the PSD-cover implication testable on labelled packet fibers.
    warning: Forgets endpoint owners unless the packet/family key is retained.
  farey_lane_scheduler: (2, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, 1, 3)
    type:    p -> q -> e=14p-q -> lane -> payload
    partial: F(p)(q)(e)(root/sum/product/power)
    LRC:     Separates affine-safe, incidence, and stress-test Farey payloads.
    warning: Forgets route labels if the payload is used without exact root data.
  pascal_path_rank_section: (2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 3, 3)
    type:    n -> k -> C(n-k-1,k), then sum_k or choose carry support
    partial: A(n)(k)
    LRC:     Keeps the Fibonacci row fiber before Zeckendorf scalarization.
    warning: Forgets route/certificate data; only carries additive row support.
  additive_basis_currency: (2, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 2, 2)
    type:    atom_system -> N -> budget -> representation_fiber
    partial: B(atoms)(N)(budget)
    LRC:     Classifies a packet as smoothing, bounded arity, or normal form.
    warning: Forgets LRC scale unless tethered to the packet root.
  runner_movie_tournament_shadow: (1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2)
    type:    S -> t -> pair_observable -> tournament
    partial: T(S)(t)(gauge)
    LRC:     Useful exploratory shadow for pairwise structure.
    warning: Forgets endpoint debt, exact M, and often the quotient fiber.
  raw_scalar_evaluation: (1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
    type:    S -> number
    partial: m(S), H(T), count(S), product(p,q)
    LRC:     Negative control for quotient guardrails.
    warning: Forgets nearly every proof-bearing argument.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: curried function carriers / proof obligations, not runners
  pairwise observable: coordinatewise retention vector over features
  switch/gauge: majority of strictly larger retention coordinates
  tie Hamiltonian path: total_curried_packet_evaluator > quotient_cocycle_derivative > residual_section_router > fejer_toeplitz_dual_functional > farey_lane_scheduler > pascal_path_rank_section > additive_basis_currency > runner_movie_tournament_shadow > raw_scalar_evaluation
  score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1, 6: 1, 7: 1, 8: 1}
  directed_3cycles=0
  scc_sizes=[1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
  hamiltonian_path_count=1
  top path:
    1. total_curried_packet_evaluator
    2. quotient_cocycle_derivative
    3. residual_section_router
    4. fejer_toeplitz_dual_functional
    5. farey_lane_scheduler
    6. pascal_path_rank_section
    7. additive_basis_currency
    8. runner_movie_tournament_shadow
    9. raw_scalar_evaluation

Proof-program takeaway:
  Treat every LRC map as a curried function.  The moment an argument is
  precomposed, evaluated, summed, or quotient-collapsed, record the lost
  coordinate as a function on the remaining fiber.  The proof target is
  not a new scalar; it is totality of this evaluator: every primitive
  LRC14 packet returns strict-safe, AP/GW boundary equality, or a named
  F7/THM-572 residual before the final scalar shadow is reached.
